From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: the HFI IRQ clears only the CM3 fault bit

a6xx_hfi_irq() clears every bit it reads from GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO, though
it only handles CM3_FAULT, the one bit the HFI interrupt is unmasked for.
The other bits there are polled for under gmu->lock: MSGQ by
a6xx_hfi_wait_for_msg_interrupt() and the OOB acks by a6xx_gmu_set_oob().
When the handler runs between the GMU setting one of them and the poll
seeing it, the answer is lost: the poll times out although the GMU
answered.

On the Adreno 740 (SM8550, AYN Odin 2 Portal) with GPU runtime PM the HFI
interrupt fires without a CM3 fault every few seconds while the GPU wakes
up and sleeps (counted in /proc/interrupts; no "GMU firmware fault" is
logged), and now and then it lands in that window:

- "Message HFI_H2F_MSG_GX_BW_PERF_VOTE id N timed out waiting for
  response", with GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO reading 0 for 10 more seconds, then
  "Unexpected message id N on the response queue" at the next message:
  the response had been in the queue all along;
- "Timeout waiting for GMU OOB set GPU_SET: 0x0" when hw_init() wakes
  the GPU. hw_init() then fails, the GPU runs uninitialized (a CP fault
  at iova 0, ring 2) and recovery hangs the display.

Clear only CM3_FAULT, as the downstream driver (kgsl) does, which writes
its HFI_IRQ_MASK to GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR rather than the status it read.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -64,7 +64,13 @@
 	struct a6xx_gmu *gmu = data;
 	u32 status;
 
-	status = gmu_read(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO);
+	/*
+	 * Only clear what this handler deals with: the HFI response (MSGQ) and
+	 * OOB ack bits are polled for, and clearing them here loses the GMU's
+	 * answer to whoever is waiting for it.
+	 */
+	status = gmu_read(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO) &
+		 A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO_CM3_FAULT;
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR, status);
 
 	if (status & A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO_CM3_FAULT) {
